1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,458
Waterbodies stretch across large areas, and tracking boundary changes by
hand is slow.

2
00:00:05,667 --> 00:00:08,625
Satellite imagery helps surface persistent water-extent change.

3
00:00:08,833 --> 00:00:12,583
But a changing shoreline alone does not prove encroachment.

4
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:21,000
Change Sentinel screens multi-date satellite observations and supporting
evidence, then records results as traceable cases for human review.

5
00:00:21,208 --> 00:00:24,958
It is a decision-support tool, not a legal authority.

6
00:00:25,875 --> 00:00:29,625
This example uses the verified Hussain Sagar study area.

7
00:00:29,833 --> 00:00:35,292
In a catalog query recorded November fifth, 2026, 640 Sentinel-2 items
were found.

8
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:39,708
After cloud filtering, 287 candidates were read successfully; none
failed.

9
00:00:39,917 --> 00:00:44,500
Accepted analysis observations span November ninth, 2022, to October
fourteenth, 2026.

10
00:00:44,708 --> 00:00:49,292
The latest usable observation was 22 days old at analysis time.

11
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:53,708
The query was live, but the imagery was not same-day.

12
00:00:54,625 --> 00:00:59,625
The pipeline compares recent observations with baseline observations
from matching calendar months.

13
00:00:59,833 --> 00:01:02,250
This reduces recurring seasonal confounding.

14
00:01:02,458 --> 00:01:10,792
The georeferenced maps show observed-water frequency on the same
EPSG:32644, 10-meter grid; they are derived rasters, not raw-color
satellite images.

15
00:01:11,708 --> 00:01:20,458
Case E N C zero zero one two records 51.9 hectares of persistent water-
extent loss candidate within a 209.29-hectare historical footprint.

16
00:01:20,667 --> 00:01:24,875
Another 28.98 hectares were classified as seasonally unmatched and
suppressed.

17
00:01:25,083 --> 00:01:28,417
Boundary-area uncertainty is plus or minus 14.63 hectares.

18
00:01:28,625 --> 00:01:31,583
These measurements describe observed change, not construction.

19
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:34,917
Evidence is mixed.

20
00:01:35,125 --> 00:01:40,125
Sentinel-1 contradicts the candidate and still detects water in recent
radar observations.

21
00:01:40,333 --> 00:01:46,583
Dynamic World also contradicts it, reporting a mean recent water
probability of zero point seven.

22
00:01:46,792 --> 00:01:51,000
JRC supports historical-water context only; its record ends in 2020.

23
00:01:51,917 --> 00:01:55,250
The case score is 50 out of 100.

24
00:01:55,458 --> 00:01:59,208
It is a heuristic review-priority score, not a probability.

25
00:01:59,417 --> 00:02:03,167
Current sources disagree, so the case remains potential change.

26
00:02:03,375 --> 00:02:05,792
No source confirms illegal encroachment.

27
00:02:06,708 --> 00:02:12,542
The stored case keeps observation dates, verified AOI provenance, source
findings and geospatial exports.

28
00:02:12,750 --> 00:02:19,000
Reviewers can inspect the GeoTIFF and GeoJSON, record decisions and
request field or cadastral verification.

29
00:02:19,917 --> 00:02:25,375
Change Sentinel helps move satellite screening into traceable
investigation while keeping uncertainty visible.

30
00:02:25,583 --> 00:02:28,542
From satellite observations to traceable waterbody investigations.
